VALUES ('ARR','published','Mortgage real-estate investment trust investing primarily in leveraged agency residential mortgage-backed securities.','ARMOUR Residential REIT finances a portfolio of agency mortgage securities largely with repurchase agreements and hedges interest-rate exposure with derivatives. Net interest spread, leverage, funding stability, prepayments and book value drive common-owner returns.','A managed portfolio of agency residential mortgage-backed securities and related hedging positions.','Interest income on mortgage assets less repurchase funding, hedge and operating costs; realized and unrealized portfolio results affect book value and distributions.','Disciplined asset selection and hedging can earn spreads and support dividends when mortgage valuations and financing markets are favorable.','ARMOUR must protect liquidity and book value through rate moves, manage leverage and duration, maintain repo access, control prepayment exposure and avoid distributing more than durable earnings.','Dividend yield alone is not the thesis. Reconcile economic return from dividends plus book-value change with leverage, hedge cost, asset spread, share issuance and management expenses.','Managed leverage can monetize agency mortgage spreads','["Agency guarantees reduce underlying credit risk.","A liquid mortgage market permits active portfolio and hedge management.","Wider spreads can create attractive reinvestment returns if liquidity is preserved."]','Leverage turns rate and spread moves into book-value risk','["Mortgage spread widening can overwhelm hedges and reduce book value.","Repo funding and margin calls can force asset sales at poor prices.","Prepayments, hedging costs, dilution and external-management expenses can impair returns."]','The thesis breaks if recurring dividends fail to offset persistent book-value erosion after hedging, funding, dilution and management costs','[{"label":"BOOK VALUE / LEVERAGE","value":"Risk base","detail":"Common equity, economic leverage, asset marks, liquidity and margin requirements"},{"label":"NET INTEREST SPREAD","value":"Earnings engine","detail":"Asset yield, repo cost, hedge cost, CPR and dollar-roll economics"},{"label":"ECONOMIC RETURN","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Dividend plus book-value change, share issuance and expense load"}]','[{"title":"Rates and mortgage spreads","level":"High","text":"Parallel and nonparallel rate moves and spread widening can damage book value.","signal":"Duration gap, hedge ratio, book value and spread marks"},{"title":"Funding and liquidity","level":"High","text":"Repo counterparties can raise haircuts or demand margin.","signal":"Cash, unencumbered assets, repo maturities and margin calls"},{"title":"Prepayment and dilution","level":"High","text":"Borrower behavior and equity issuance can reduce per-share returns.","signal":"CPR, premium amortization, shares issued and book value per share"}]','[{"title":"Economic return","text":"Measure dividends together with quarterly change in book value per share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Liquidity stress test","text":"Track leverage, repo maturity, unencumbered collateral and hedge cash needs under adverse rate moves.","impact":"BEAR CASE"}]','["What portion of reported earnings is repeatable after hedge and financing costs?","How much liquidity is available for a sharp mortgage-spread widening?","Has equity issuance increased or diluted book value per share?"]','AGNC Investment, Annaly Capital Management, Dynex Capital, Orchid Island Capital and other agency mortgage REITs.','2026-02-18','2026-08-04T21:06:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
