VALUES ('ARRY','published','Global provider of utility-scale solar tracking, fixed-tilt, foundation, software and related service solutions.','Array Technologies supplies systems that position utility-scale solar modules and support project construction and operation. Bookings, backlog conversion, project timing, steel and logistics costs, product reliability and geographic mix drive results.','Single-axis solar trackers, fixed-tilt systems, foundation solutions, controls, software, components and services.','Equipment and system revenue is recognized as project obligations are fulfilled, with additional parts, software and service economics.','Utility-scale solar deployment, tracker adoption and broader site solutions can expand volume and value per project.','Array must win bankable projects, convert backlog on schedule, manage steel and freight, preserve product quality, navigate trade policy and collect from concentrated developers and contractors.','Backlog is not cash: verify cancellation rights, pricing, delivery schedule, customer credit, working-capital needs and margin after commodity, tariff and warranty costs.','Scale and integrated site solutions can gain with solar buildout','["A large installed base and project history support bankability.","Tracking can increase energy yield relative to fixed systems in suitable projects.","Foundations, software and services can increase value per site."]','Project volatility and commoditization pressure margins','["Permitting, interconnection, financing and customer delays can shift or cancel projects.","Steel, freight, tariffs and pricing competition can compress gross margin.","Warranty, design or installation failures can create significant claims."]','The thesis breaks if backlog and solar demand grow without durable margin, cash conversion and acceptable warranty performance','[{"label":"BOOKINGS / BACKLOG","value":"Demand visibility","detail":"New awards, cancellations, timing, geography, customer and product mix"},{"label":"GROSS MARGIN","value":"Execution test","detail":"Price, steel, freight, tariffs, mix, utilization and warranty cost"},{"label":"WORKING CAPITAL","value":"Cash conversion","detail":"Inventory, receivables, customer deposits, project milestones and operating cash flow"}]','[{"title":"Project timing and policy","level":"High","text":"Solar economics depend on permitting, interconnection, tax, trade and financing conditions.","signal":"Bookings, pushouts, cancellations and customer financing"},{"title":"Input cost and competition","level":"High","text":"Steel, freight, tariffs and aggressive bids can compress margin.","signal":"Price-cost, gross margin, supplier terms and imports"},{"title":"Product and warranty","level":"Medium","text":"Field failures can require repairs and damage bankability.","signal":"Warranty reserve, claims, redesigns and customer acceptance"}]','[{"title":"Backlog quality","text":"Track firm orders, cancellation terms, expected shipment dates and customer credit before treating backlog as revenue.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Cash-backed margin","text":"Require reported gross profit to convert into operating cash after inventory and receivable investment.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["How much backlog is fixed-price and exposed to cost inflation?","Which project delays are timing shifts versus economic cancellations?","Do added foundations and software improve margin and retention?"]','Nextracker, GameChange Solar, PV Hardware, FTC Solar, fixed-tilt providers and vertically integrated solar contractors.','2026-02-25','2026-08-04T21:06:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
